<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">The Tale of Igor's Campaign</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 12th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Lay of Igor's Campaign, Song of Igor's Campaign</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tale of Igor's Campaign is an anonymous Old East Slavic epic poem, usually dated to the late 12th century. It tells of the failed raid of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/igor-svyatoslavich">Prince Igor</a> Sviatoslavich of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/novhorod-siverskyi">Novgorod-Seversky</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cumans">Cumans</a> in 1185 and calls on the Rus' princes to unite. Its only known <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a> was found in the 1790s and burned in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> fire of 1812.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/the-tale-of-igors-campaign.jpg" alt="The Tale of Igor's Campaign" width="320" height="457" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Slovo_o_polku_igoreve_1800.djvu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
